[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelpmahan/chainspot-toolkit/pulls/1","id":4942593543,"node_id":"PR_kwDOVNKKCc8AAAABJpn-Bw","html_url":"https://github.com/samuelpmahan/chainspot-toolkit/pull/1","diff_url":"https://github.com/samuelpmahan/chainspot-toolkit/pull/1.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/samuelpmahan/chainspot-toolkit/pull/1.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelpmahan/chainspot-toolkit/issues/1","number":1,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Add receipt-gated Rebalancer execution emulator and measured allocation controls","user":{"login":"samuelpmahan","id":32501459,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyNTAxNDU5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32501459?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelpmahan","html_url":"https://github.com/samuelpmahan","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelpmahan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelpmahan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelpmahan/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelpmahan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelpmahan/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelpmahan/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelpmahan/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelpmahan/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelpmahan/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"The native Rebalancer experiment could recommend assignments but required manual dispatch. This adds an opt-in bounded local Python worker emulator around the existing solver: receipt-gated dependency release, independent-worker review, bounded repair, attempt fencing, continuous backfill, and resumable interruption recovery. It includes write-once completion records so completed outcomes survive older mutable state/event projections.\n\nAll changes stay under `experiments/rebalancer/`. The native solver wrapper, original recipe, adversarial probe, requirements and historical manual-run evidence are preserved. Platform and algorithm production lanes are untouched. This is local worker emulation; it does not control live agents or establish agent throughput.\n\n### Executed evidence\n\n- Final candidate: **54 Python tests passed**, including actual SIGKILL/recovery cases; five original native adversarial cases passed.\n- **30 measured runs**: six logical workers, dynamic / balanced fixed / tuned static policies, declared-delay and zero-delay scenarios, five repetitions each.\n- Independent persisted-data audit: **540 accepted receipts, 210 native solve receipts, 1,050 exact source quotations, zero mismatches**; every run completed eight final roots after one repair.\n- Six later-reverted mutable projections were restored without worker execution; their completion records remained byte-for-byte unchanged.\n- Broader Node suite: **39 passed, 6 failed**, exactly matching untouched-base missing-fixture failures.\n\n| Scenario | Dynamic median wall | Fixed 3/3 | Tuned fixed 2/4 |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|\n| Declared delays | 1.5438 s | 1.6995 s | 1.6300 s |\n| Zero delay | 1.1662 s | 1.1050 s | 1.2224 s |\n\nEarlier native tests twice rejected a nonoptimal solver score before dispatch; those failure logs are retained. The final 30-run sample had no such rejection. The comparison runner now retries only that exact rejection with at most three sessions and includes failed-session costs in wall time. Earlier diagnostic/partial comparisons are retained and excluded from these figures.\n\nSee [RESULTS.md](https://github.com/samuelpmahan/chainspot-toolkit/blob/989c295717511c812b69beda5d125817ffc054c9/experiments/rebalancer/RESULTS.md) for commands, observed ranges, timing definitions, recovery boundaries and limitations. `Rebalancer-Execution-Evidence-20261020.zip` is delivered alongside this checkpoint with raw events, decision snapshots, native bundles, receipts, measurements, audit scripts and test logs. Timing is observational in a shared container, and review/extraction share a parser.\n\nDraft for review; no main-branch merge, algorithm integration or live-agent speedup is claimed.","created_at":"2026-10-20T21:14:57Z","updated_at":"2026-10-20T21:14:57Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"69f9d5ec1475adf2f78377fa2c090b16157eaad0","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":true,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelpmahan/chainspot-toolkit/pulls/1/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelpmahan/chainspot-toolkit/pulls/1/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelpmahan/chainspot-toolkit/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelpmahan/chainspot-toolkit/issues/1/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelpmahan/chainspot-toolkit/statuses/989c295717511c812b69beda5d125817ffc054c9","head":{"label":"samuelpmahan:codex/rebalancer-execution-loop-20261020","ref":"codex/rebalancer-execution-loop-20261020","sha":"989c295717511c812b69beda5d125817ffc054c9","user":{"login":"samuelpmahan","id":32501459,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyNTAxNDU5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32501459?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelpmahan","html_url":"https://github.com/samuelpmahan","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelpmahan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelpmahan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelpmahan/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelpmahan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelpmahan/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelpmahan/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/u